#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""term-notify: pushes "an agent needs you" to your phone when an agent in tmux stops for you.

It watches the tmux pane option `@agent` (written by the omp extension and the Claude Code and Codex hooks) and
posts {secret, session_ref, kind} to the relay named in each pairing file. Nothing else leaves the machine.

    term-notify install [--no-start]   copy to ~/.local/share/term/notify, start at login (LaunchAgent / systemd --user)
    term-notify uninstall [--purge]    stop and remove; --purge also deletes the pairing files
    term-notify run                    the watcher itself (what the service runs)
    term-notify once                   one pass: send what is due now, then exit
    term-notify status                 service, tmux and pairings; exit 1 when something needs fixing

Python 3.8+, standard library only. See README.md next to this file.
"""
